# Design Plan — Long-Endurance Drone Battery (Case t8_r2)

## Objective (verbatim from task)
- Energy density >= 446.18 Wh/kg (contract-caliber: discharge energy / layer-stack mass, electrolyte excluded)
- 5C discharge: capacity retention >= 90% (5C cap / 1C cap, same parameters, DFN)
- Cell mass <= 40 g (layer-stack mass; 40 g = 0.04 kg)

## Objective decomposition & trade-offs
1. ED >= 446.18 Wh/kg — decides stack composition: requires high active/inactive mass ratio (thin current collectors, thin separator, high electrode density, low porosity) and high mean voltage. Chen2020 baseline geometry (75.6 µm NMC811 / 85.2 µm graphite, 12 µm separator, 16/12 µm CC) contract-ED ≈ 400-415 (to be measured) → gap ~30-45 Wh/kg.
2. retention_5c >= 0.9 — rate capability: needs small particles, thin electrodes, high-electrolyte-transport (σ, D, t+). Trade-off with ED: thick electrodes raise ED but 5C retention decays via diffusion overpotential; keep electrodes moderate (≤ ~90 µm pos) and push transport instead.
3. mass_kg <= 0.04 — baseline stack ≈ 43.5 g (area 0.1027 m²) → reduce electrode area (width 1.58 → ~1.45 m) or trim inactive mass; ED/retention are area-independent (ratio metrics), so area is the free mass lever. 
- Priority: ED and retention are the binding pair (Pareto); mass satisfiable geometrically.
- Expected trade-off direction: ED + (thickness) ↔ retention −; retention + (small particles/σ) ↔ ED neutral-or-positive (transport levers don't add mass) → prefer transport levers before thickness extremes.

## Candidate strategy
- R1: baseline characterization (Chen2020, no overrides): 1C DFN, calc-energy, 5C DFN, 4C-charge 45°C safety. Establishes gap magnitude + ceiling assessment.
- R2-R4 (architecture+formulation): 2-4 variants/round: thin CCs (12/8 → 6/4 µm), thin separator (12 → 8-9 µm), porosity trim (pos 0.335 → 0.30 / neg 0.25 → 0.26), N/P tune (via negative thickness), particle radius trim (pos 5.2 → 3.5 µm, neg 5.9 → 4 µm), electrolyte σ=1.2-1.3 S/m, D=2.6e-10, t+=0.35 (literature high-conductivity LiPF6-carbonate; Valøen & Reimers 2005 JES 152 A882; Nyman 2008).
- Ceiling assessment after R1: if best-case architecture+formulation ceiling < 446.18 → escalate Stage 2: system candidates OKane2022 (graphite+SiOx, higher anode capacity) → possibly invent materials.
- Final candidate: 5C retention + safety exam (4C charge 45 °C, plating) + mass check.

## Budget allocation
- R1 baseline: 4 sims. R2-R6: ~4 variants × 4 sims each ≈ 16 sims. System-switch rounds (if any): +2 rounds. Total target ≤ 8 rounds, ~30 sims, all seconds-minutes scale (SPMe/DFN).
- True compute (real_compute=false): skipped; endorse entry records skip.

## Risk & fallback
- Risk 1: 446.18 above NMC811/graphite architecture ceiling even under aggressive levers → escalation to Stage 2 (SiOx anode system or cathode composition); if still below → three-strike questioning → honest negative or boundary note.
- Risk 2: 5C retention 90% not met due to electrolyte transport limit in DFN → formulation overrides (σ/D/t+) then particle/thickness trim; coating skip.
- Risk 3: 4C-charge plating (safety gate) — anode overpotential at 4C charge on thin graphite → trim negative thickness (raise electrode:A ratio... no, plating risk rises when anode thin/imbalanced) — fix via smaller negative particles + higher σ + N/P.
- Risk 4: mass > 40 g at final stack → reduce area (mechanical, no re-sim needed since ratio metrics invariant... wait — capacity changes but ED/retention same; but calc-energy must be re-run with new area for the mass_kg evidence).
- Three-strike triggers with same cause → escalate questioning (system/boundary/metric), per protocol.

## References (direction → source)
- High-capacity anode (SiOx/graphite) raises cell ED → Obrovac & Chevrier, Chem. Rev. 114 (2014) 11444–11502 (alloy anodes) [real]; OKane et al. 2022 parameterization (SiOx-containing NMC cell, J. Electrochem. Soc.) [real — OKane2022 is a published JES parameter set].
- NMC811/graphite cell design envelope → Chen et al. 2020, J. Electrochem. Soc. 167, 080534 (Chen2020 parameterization basis) [real].
- Electrolyte transport ceiling (σ, D, t+ of LiPF6 carbonate blends) → Valøen & Reimers 2005, J. Electrochem. Soc. 152, A882 [real]; Nyman et al. 2008, Electrochim. Acta 53, 6356 [real].
- Li-metal / next-gen drone-cell ED paths → Lin, Liu & Cui, Nat. Nanotechnol. 12 (2017) 194–206 [real]; drone battery roadmaps → domain experience (no precise source).

